   {
    "title": "Full HP Website",
    "description": "FULL-HP is web application which serves as a one-stop source for information and current news regarding video games. Users are able create a pro􀃺le, login, and to subscribe to their favorite games. Application users also have the ability to participate in group chats or in private messaging. Information from multiple sources (IGN, Steam, Twitter, and Twitch) provide a single place to consume gaming information. Additionally, the application facilitates the viewing of live Twitch streams of a video game of their choice.\n\nRoles / Responsibilities\n- Responsible for managing Git-􀃻ow and repositories for projects.\n- Created and maintained the CI/CD pipelines hosted on AWS for both Java back-end and Angular front-end.\n- Leveraged AWS Relational Database Service to provide a cloud-hosted persistence solution.\n- Assisted with the creation of Angular components and services to provide front-to-back end connections.\n- Employed the Spring Framework to reduce the amount of boilerplate code needed for developing web applications.\n- Utilized Spring MVC to create controllers and methods to handle HTTP requests and responses.\n- Collaborated with team members to connect Angular front-end services to a Java back-end API.\n- Participated in daily stand-ups with team members as part of an Agile workflow.\n\nEnvironment / Technologies\nJava, Angular, TypeScript, Hibernate, Spring, CodePipeline, CodeBuild, Elastic Beanstalk, EC2, RDS, Git,\nContinuous Integration, HTML, Sass, CSS, Bootstrap",
